    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_11cd0f616c4c218f18fba21942d03c0eb8e7cfe0a1e7153189e6f2b561265218",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under the virtual-isometry coupling, periodically indexed eigenangles converge pointwise across dimensions; the sine-product calculation rewrites each finite normalized characteristic polynomial in the same symmetric zero-product coordinates as the limit; and logarithmic rigidity makes the paired tails uniformly summable. Fixed-factor convergence and Montel's theorem therefore upgrade spectral convergence to almost-sure compact-uniform convergence to an entire function with the limiting sine-process zeros.",
