      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_70018485bef41df21b64d7420987320d96fcf52ee0b27476851383619aa32497",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Concentration estimates become a common rigidity layer for global analytic control: phase concentration on a grid and determinantal count tails are patched with the central coupling to prove logarithmic location rigidity; that rigidity makes paired product tails summable, while a finer positive-negative block decomposition turns determinantal count fluctuations into exponential and then L^p control of logarithmic-derivative tails, licensing moment passage through infinite sums.",
