    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7f61642dbb7bcae14aed8ffccc519418f53e56ecaacc4734da85c5df6970b255",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The off-real resolvent test belongs to H^{1/2}, so the centered sine-process resolvent is a legitimate linear statistic and equals a corrected logarithmic derivative. Mesoscopic dilation preserves the critical blue-noise covariance while pushing higher cumulants to vanishing frequency regions; the scaling identity then yields a Gaussian analytic-field candidate, and covariance-based continuity, holomorphicity, and tightness upgrade finite-dimensional convergence to compact-uniform convergence in law.",
