    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a3b3fe73e602d35a45bb9d91e4f4103821328b901f242535348bba3b54a83688",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Uniform off-real logarithmic-derivative control is the integrability gate connecting finite and limiting algebraic identities. Integrating the logarithmic derivative along zero-free paths and controlling local counts gives uniform moments of balanced ratios; these moments provide uniform integrability for passing finite-n ratio expectations to ξ_∞ and justify Cauchy-integral differentiation. The finite CUE Giambelli determinant can therefore be transported to ξ_∞ and differentiated into arbitrary joint logarithmic-derivative moments, with combinatorial cancellations compressing the raw derivative expansion.",
